WEBVTT

00:00:04.130 --> 00:00:05.940
Sayako! Sayako!

00:00:09.240 --> 00:00:12.290
I couldn't do anything!

00:00:12.290 --> 00:00:14.040
All I could do was watch.

00:00:15.830 --> 00:00:17.650
I'm so weak.

00:00:20.080 --> 00:00:23.330
Magical Girl War Nurse Kurumi!

00:00:23.330 --> 00:00:25.000
Bear!

00:00:44.860 --> 00:00:47.690
Asuka-san?

00:00:50.310 --> 00:00:51.650
Um...

00:00:52.670 --> 00:00:54.360
It's been a while.

00:00:59.190 --> 00:01:02.860
Make sure you protect me from now on, okay?

00:01:06.290 --> 00:01:08.050
This is sudden,

00:01:08.050 --> 00:01:12.250
but we have another transfer
student to introduce to you!

00:01:13.030 --> 00:01:18.840
I'll be learning here at this school
with you all starting today.

00:01:18.840 --> 00:01:20.470
My name is Mugen Kurumi.

00:01:21.460 --> 00:01:24.430
It's nice to meet you all.

00:02:58.490 --> 00:03:01.360
<b>Northern Mexico, Tijuana</b>

00:03:30.570 --> 00:03:33.980
Magical Girl Just Cause Mia.

00:03:35.010 --> 00:03:38.940
It feels strange when you
transform right in front of me.

00:03:38.940 --> 00:03:43.280
That's because of the Magical Girls'
 prosopagnosia inducing field.

00:03:43.280 --> 00:03:45.320
The one that keeps anyone from recognizing you

00:03:45.320 --> 00:03:47.980
as the person you were before you transformed,
unless you reveal your identity.

00:03:47.980 --> 00:03:51.660
It still feels weird,
and we <i>know</i> your identity.

00:03:52.330 --> 00:03:56.120
I think it's because my 
magical power is too strong.

00:03:56.690 --> 00:03:57.880
Now then...

00:03:58.570 --> 00:04:00.840
It's time to get going.

00:04:05.280 --> 00:04:07.310
I'll take point.

00:04:15.380 --> 00:04:17.210
Just like our source said.

00:04:17.210 --> 00:04:19.440
This is a drug cartel stronghold.

00:04:42.260 --> 00:04:43.660
Nice work.

00:04:43.660 --> 00:04:46.540
The power of that thing amazes
me no matter how many times I see it.

00:04:46.540 --> 00:04:50.300
Specifically, it's a magically-induced
increase in penetrating power.

00:04:50.300 --> 00:04:51.910
It went right through the walls,

00:04:51.910 --> 00:04:54.340
the door, a table with a metal
plate embedded in it,

00:04:54.340 --> 00:04:59.630
and clean through NIJ Level IIIa body armor.

00:04:59.630 --> 00:05:00.900
That's crazy.

00:05:00.900 --> 00:05:03.480
Come on, stay focused.

00:05:09.660 --> 00:05:11.920
There's one more in the back.

00:05:13.050 --> 00:05:14.620
No traps.

00:05:21.960 --> 00:05:25.480
278867...

00:05:25.480 --> 00:05:34.140
98962627886792...

00:05:34.140 --> 00:05:35.310
Numbers?

00:05:35.310 --> 00:05:37.560
Who are you?

00:05:37.560 --> 00:05:39.730
We're not criminals.

00:05:50.330 --> 00:05:51.130
Ba...

00:05:52.060 --> 00:05:53.920
The Babel Brigade...

00:05:54.240 --> 00:05:57.930
A more terrible war...

00:06:01.920 --> 00:06:04.420
Wh... What the hell was that?

00:06:04.820 --> 00:06:09.230
Looks like there's more
to this than a simple drug cartel.

00:06:09.800 --> 00:06:12.140
If magic's involved,

00:06:12.140 --> 00:06:14.130
that changes things.

00:06:14.130 --> 00:06:15.960
It doesn't change a thing.

00:06:17.560 --> 00:06:21.910
Crushing these fuckers is our job.

00:06:22.560 --> 00:06:27.570
<b>A More Terrible War</b>

00:06:32.500 --> 00:06:36.330
I heard you were with the SDF,
researching magical combat.

00:06:36.330 --> 00:06:38.850
I'm still going to high school.

00:06:39.600 --> 00:06:41.840
I didn't expect you to just transfer here.

00:06:41.980 --> 00:06:46.640
Iizuka-san's got a lot of
influence in strange places.

00:06:46.640 --> 00:06:51.190
When I told him that if he
couldn't get me into your school,

00:06:51.190 --> 00:06:54.530
I was going to quit the Self-Defense Force,
 he got it done fast.

00:06:55.180 --> 00:06:57.630
I'm half-kidding.

00:06:58.640 --> 00:07:02.700
Were you thinking I sound like a stalker?

00:07:02.700 --> 00:07:03.630
No,

00:07:03.630 --> 00:07:04.980
I was just a little surprised.

00:07:07.680 --> 00:07:09.700
That Halloween-class...

00:07:10.400 --> 00:07:13.010
The situation's changing.

00:07:13.010 --> 00:07:16.160
But it's not my problem anymore.

00:07:16.640 --> 00:07:18.930
The enemy disagrees.

00:07:18.930 --> 00:07:22.120
It's better if we're both in one place
as much as possible.

00:07:23.070 --> 00:07:26.300
If we could live in the same place, too...

00:07:26.300 --> 00:07:27.460
Hey!

00:07:28.390 --> 00:07:31.680
You two transfer students
are friends already, huh?

00:07:32.620 --> 00:07:34.770
I'm Makino Nozomi.

00:07:34.770 --> 00:07:36.430
This is Hata Sayako.

00:07:36.430 --> 00:07:37.690
Hi...

00:07:40.010 --> 00:07:42.450
You're Asuka-san's friends, right?

00:07:42.450 --> 00:07:44.100
Yay! Yay! Yay!

00:07:44.100 --> 00:07:45.360
Yes, I guess.

00:07:46.820 --> 00:07:48.570
"You guess"?

00:07:50.830 --> 00:07:54.420
I'm Asuka-san's best friend.

00:07:56.350 --> 00:07:58.250
Nice to meet you.

00:07:58.250 --> 00:07:59.900
Yay! Yay! Yay!

00:08:08.170 --> 00:08:11.940
Asuka-san, the Salisbury
steak today is great.

00:08:11.940 --> 00:08:13.630
Want some?

00:08:13.840 --> 00:08:16.290
Okay, just a little.

00:08:16.810 --> 00:08:18.760
Say, "Aah!"

00:08:29.550 --> 00:08:32.450
You two are really close, huh?

00:08:32.670 --> 00:08:33.610
Yes.

00:08:33.610 --> 00:08:34.570
Hey,

00:08:34.570 --> 00:08:37.680
so exactly what is Asuka-san to you?

00:08:37.680 --> 00:08:39.160
My goddess.

00:08:40.730 --> 00:08:42.590
Deep!

00:08:42.590 --> 00:08:45.250
So Asuka-san, what do you think of Kurumi-san?

00:08:47.470 --> 00:08:49.050
Let me see...

00:08:49.050 --> 00:08:51.470
She's somebody close to me
that I can count on.

00:08:52.660 --> 00:08:55.140
She's not just kind. She's strong.

00:08:55.610 --> 00:08:59.430
There are lots of times when I've been in 
trouble and only made it out because of her.

00:08:59.430 --> 00:09:00.970
Asuka-san...

00:09:06.920 --> 00:09:08.110
Sayako?

00:09:09.530 --> 00:09:10.770
It's okay.

00:09:10.770 --> 00:09:12.750
Come on, inhale.

00:09:13.260 --> 00:09:14.500
Exhale...

00:09:16.530 --> 00:09:18.850
What happened to her?

00:09:19.600 --> 00:09:22.250
She was at the scene of 
the Iidabashi terrorist attack.

00:09:22.250 --> 00:09:24.760
Fortunately, she was unharmed, but...

00:09:26.640 --> 00:09:28.190
Sorry.

00:09:28.190 --> 00:09:29.840
I'm fine now.

00:09:30.350 --> 00:09:33.490
Things have been so crazy lately, right?

00:09:33.490 --> 00:09:35.430
I wonder if there's something we can do.

00:09:35.430 --> 00:09:37.050
"Something?"

00:09:37.360 --> 00:09:38.340
You know,

00:09:38.340 --> 00:09:39.820
there's that stuff they sell online.

00:09:39.820 --> 00:09:41.140
Self-defense items.

00:09:41.140 --> 00:09:42.270
Bulletproof vests.

00:09:42.430 --> 00:09:43.740
If you don't train,

00:09:43.740 --> 00:09:45.280
a bulletproof vest is really heavy.

00:09:45.280 --> 00:09:48.070
It's better to just run away.

00:09:48.070 --> 00:09:49.320
That's right.

00:09:49.320 --> 00:09:51.230
Let the police handle the dangerous stuff.

00:09:52.050 --> 00:09:53.390
I see.

00:09:53.390 --> 00:09:54.230
Well,

00:09:54.230 --> 00:09:57.320
if things get really bad,
the Magical Girls will save us, right?

00:10:07.130 --> 00:10:08.040
Huh?

00:10:08.040 --> 00:10:09.630
Did I say something weird?

00:10:10.460 --> 00:10:11.840
I'm sorry.

00:10:11.840 --> 00:10:13.720
No, that's not it.

00:10:13.720 --> 00:10:15.970
Let's keep things a little
more cheerful, okay?

00:10:16.170 --> 00:10:16.960
That's right.

00:10:16.960 --> 00:10:18.050
Cheerful.

00:10:19.060 --> 00:10:20.010
Right?

00:10:22.910 --> 00:10:25.600
Hey, Kurumi-san, do you swim?

00:10:25.900 --> 00:10:27.750
Yes, a bit.

00:10:27.750 --> 00:10:31.610
Why don't we all go to the pool Sunday?

00:10:32.320 --> 00:10:33.310
The pool?

00:10:33.310 --> 00:10:35.290
Yeah, the pool!

00:10:36.190 --> 00:10:39.200
The pool, where water
droplets bounce off soft skin!

00:10:39.200 --> 00:10:43.910
Where you get to admire rippling
muscles and beautiful curves!

00:10:49.060 --> 00:10:51.630
I don't know about beautiful curves,

00:10:51.630 --> 00:10:54.030
but I do like the idea of swimming.

00:10:54.030 --> 00:10:55.630
If Asuka-san's going...

00:10:57.120 --> 00:10:58.760
I'm fine with that.

00:10:58.760 --> 00:11:00.780
Okay, great!

00:11:00.780 --> 00:11:01.920
Yay!

00:11:10.230 --> 00:11:15.530
That Makino Nozomi
girl sure is pushy, huh?

00:11:15.650 --> 00:11:19.780
But she's a good girl.
She keeps everyone cheerful.

00:11:29.710 --> 00:11:34.570
This school's got a ton of
workout machines, huh?

00:11:34.570 --> 00:11:38.100
There aren't a lot of people here,
either, so it's easy to use them.

00:11:38.320 --> 00:11:40.400
You're a researcher.

00:11:40.400 --> 00:11:42.280
Do you need to train?

00:11:42.280 --> 00:11:44.190
I'm a Magical Girl.

00:11:44.190 --> 00:11:46.560
I never know what will happen.

00:11:47.210 --> 00:11:48.980
You're strong.

00:11:48.980 --> 00:11:51.020
I'm not strong.

00:11:51.340 --> 00:11:57.610
Then how can you still fight so
optimistically after that awful battle?

00:11:59.330 --> 00:12:00.610
Because...

00:12:03.320 --> 00:12:05.390
Hey, does it stink?

00:12:05.390 --> 00:12:07.390
I smell vomit.

00:12:07.390 --> 00:12:09.080
So do I.

00:12:09.080 --> 00:12:10.600
That's strange.

00:12:10.600 --> 00:12:13.040
I know we washed her.

00:12:13.040 --> 00:12:15.090
Want to wash her again?

00:12:15.090 --> 00:12:16.270
There's no point.

00:12:16.270 --> 00:12:18.640
She won't smell better no matter
how many times you do it.

00:12:18.640 --> 00:12:21.480
Why not just stay here all day?

00:12:21.480 --> 00:12:24.010
Nobody wants you stinking
up the classroom.

00:12:24.650 --> 00:12:26.850
Please... just...

00:12:28.100 --> 00:12:30.380
You're garbage.
Garbage doesn't breathe.

00:12:32.200 --> 00:12:36.730
I like myself now that I can
transform into a Magical Girl.

00:12:37.320 --> 00:12:40.650
I don't like the person
I was when I couldn't.

00:12:42.180 --> 00:12:43.870
What about you, Asuka-san?

00:12:44.090 --> 00:12:47.060
You said you wanted
to quit being a Magical Girl,

00:12:47.060 --> 00:12:49.330
but you're still in excellent shape.

00:12:50.000 --> 00:12:52.610
I like keeping myself in shape.

00:12:53.490 --> 00:12:55.420
Is that really all?

00:12:57.280 --> 00:12:58.280
I'm scared.

00:12:58.830 --> 00:13:00.370
Maybe.

00:13:00.660 --> 00:13:01.760
Scared?

00:13:02.200 --> 00:13:03.590
Of the enemy?

00:13:04.520 --> 00:13:05.390
No.

00:13:05.980 --> 00:13:08.040
Of becoming weak.

00:13:32.760 --> 00:13:33.730
This way.

00:13:34.350 --> 00:13:36.110
What's this about?

00:13:47.620 --> 00:13:50.210
Welcome, Master!

00:13:50.210 --> 00:13:51.470
Welcome.

00:13:54.200 --> 00:13:57.870
They're both ace members of the JGSDF.

00:13:57.870 --> 00:13:59.460
These are the members of M Squad,

00:13:59.460 --> 00:14:03.910
an elite unit within the Special Forces Group,
specializing in magical combat.

00:14:04.370 --> 00:14:05.700
I'm Shima.

00:14:05.700 --> 00:14:07.610
Nice to meet you.

00:14:08.250 --> 00:14:09.360
Kaede.

00:14:10.620 --> 00:14:13.370
This is M Squad's secret base.

00:14:13.920 --> 00:14:16.760
We can't do anything too crazy
in a government-owned building.

00:14:16.760 --> 00:14:19.060
But why a maid café?

00:14:19.060 --> 00:14:21.460
I didn't exactly sign up for this, either!

00:14:21.460 --> 00:14:24.460
Calm down, Kaede! Calm down!

00:14:24.460 --> 00:14:27.480
There's a staircase in the back
that leads to sub-basement B2.

00:14:27.480 --> 00:14:30.140
There's a training room and an armory.

00:14:29.060 --> 00:14:30.140
Hey.

00:14:30.730 --> 00:14:32.240
We've been over this.

00:14:32.240 --> 00:14:33.790
I'm not...

00:14:33.790 --> 00:14:38.110
There's been a huge increase
in magical item smuggling lately.

00:14:38.110 --> 00:14:39.890
The war's over.

00:14:40.040 --> 00:14:41.380
That's right.

00:14:41.380 --> 00:14:42.850
The war's over.

00:14:42.850 --> 00:14:44.980
And a new order is being born.

00:14:45.820 --> 00:14:51.450
Criminal spirits are trading magic
for rare materials from Earth.

00:14:51.710 --> 00:14:53.660
Leftover remnants from the war?

00:14:53.660 --> 00:14:57.810
"Remnants" isn't the right
way of looking at it anymore.

00:14:57.810 --> 00:15:00.500
They were able to modify
that Halloween-class.

00:15:00.500 --> 00:15:02.600
Somebody big is backing them.

00:15:03.190 --> 00:15:04.970
And that's not all.

00:15:04.970 --> 00:15:07.880
We're even seeing illegal Magical Girls.

00:15:08.450 --> 00:15:10.920
The world's rules have changed.

00:15:10.920 --> 00:15:15.100
And a new world needs new power.

00:15:16.070 --> 00:15:18.300
It needs your power,

00:15:18.600 --> 00:15:21.050
Magical Girl Rapture.

00:15:22.600 --> 00:15:23.840
I...

00:15:41.450 --> 00:15:43.790
Magical...

00:15:43.790 --> 00:15:44.850
What?

00:15:44.850 --> 00:15:46.700
What did you say?

00:15:46.700 --> 00:15:49.140
Magical Girl...

00:15:49.140 --> 00:15:50.490
Prey...

00:15:50.490 --> 00:15:53.610
Remake the world...

00:15:53.610 --> 00:15:54.810
The world?

00:15:54.810 --> 00:15:56.260
Not the Japanese government?

00:15:57.450 --> 00:15:59.560
New organization...

00:15:59.560 --> 00:16:02.110
Library of Babel...

00:16:02.110 --> 00:16:04.230
Babel Brigade...

00:16:04.230 --> 00:16:08.410
A more... terrible... war...

00:16:09.270 --> 00:16:12.830
Magical Girls are prey, huh?

00:16:12.830 --> 00:16:15.890
This case is a bigger
deal than I thought, huh?

00:16:15.890 --> 00:16:20.000
We'll have to change all our
assumptions about this enemy.

00:16:20.000 --> 00:16:24.260
What can we do against
an enemy like this?

00:16:24.260 --> 00:16:27.170
We're cops.

00:16:27.170 --> 00:16:29.630
Magic or not,

00:16:29.630 --> 00:16:32.170
we just do our jobs.

00:16:32.770 --> 00:16:36.530
So that normal people can live in peace.

00:16:51.150 --> 00:16:53.160
What a beautiful sight.

00:16:53.380 --> 00:16:54.510
Nozo-chan,

00:16:54.510 --> 00:16:55.780
you're such an old man.

00:16:56.270 --> 00:16:59.870
Well, our own forces are just as strong.

00:17:09.950 --> 00:17:11.250
Beautiful!

00:17:11.660 --> 00:17:13.420
Nozo-chan...

00:17:13.420 --> 00:17:14.480
Aw,

00:17:14.480 --> 00:17:16.210
"beautiful" is going too far.

00:17:16.210 --> 00:17:17.510
Right, Asuka-san?

00:17:22.750 --> 00:17:24.810
Asuka-san, wait!

00:17:25.440 --> 00:17:28.190
Okay! Me, too!

00:17:36.090 --> 00:17:36.980
Hey.

00:17:38.290 --> 00:17:40.860
Thank you for coming, guys.

00:17:41.540 --> 00:17:43.460
What's that for?

00:17:44.410 --> 00:17:47.640
Sayako's still pretty down.

00:17:49.020 --> 00:17:52.120
She's a total four-eyes who 
always has her nose in a book,

00:17:52.120 --> 00:17:54.480
but she likes to swim.

00:17:54.480 --> 00:17:56.920
Do her glasses have
anything to do with anything?

00:17:57.490 --> 00:17:59.780
I'm glad you came.

00:18:00.690 --> 00:18:02.100
Why?

00:18:02.100 --> 00:18:07.210
She likes cool girls like you and me.

00:18:07.210 --> 00:18:09.440
I think it makes her more excited.

00:18:10.190 --> 00:18:11.560
Cool?

00:18:13.650 --> 00:18:15.400
Hey, where is she?

00:18:17.020 --> 00:18:19.500
Is that her?

00:18:20.700 --> 00:18:23.450
She dives?

00:18:23.450 --> 00:18:24.280
No,

00:18:24.280 --> 00:18:25.540
she's never mentioned it before.

00:19:22.040 --> 00:19:25.010
I'm glad nothing bad happened.

00:19:25.010 --> 00:19:26.690
Really.

00:19:26.690 --> 00:19:27.800
I'm sorry.

00:19:28.100 --> 00:19:29.760
You did a great job with that dive.

00:19:30.940 --> 00:19:34.550
I'm tired of being so scared I can't move.

00:19:37.560 --> 00:19:40.650
<i>Everyone's moving forward, aren't they?</i>

00:19:42.320 --> 00:19:44.100
Feel better?

00:19:44.100 --> 00:19:44.830
Yeah.

00:19:44.830 --> 00:19:46.120
I bet.

00:19:46.120 --> 00:19:49.050
You were staring at lots
of crotches at the pool.

00:19:49.050 --> 00:19:50.750
I was not.

00:19:50.750 --> 00:19:52.040
You were, too.

00:19:52.450 --> 00:19:54.950
We know you're a perv.

00:19:54.950 --> 00:19:56.470
Nozo-chan!

00:19:58.140 --> 00:20:00.260
What's wrong, Asuka-san?

00:20:01.600 --> 00:20:02.810
Nothing...

00:20:03.510 --> 00:20:07.060
I was just wondering if it was
okay to do things like this.

00:20:09.330 --> 00:20:11.250
Of course it is.

00:20:11.250 --> 00:20:14.480
Otherwise, you'll regret it when you grow
up and work eighty-hour weeks.

00:20:14.480 --> 00:20:15.730
Eighty-hour weeks?

00:20:16.000 --> 00:20:17.930
You need to have
fun with your life right now!

00:20:17.930 --> 00:20:20.190
So let's do this again!

00:20:22.750 --> 00:20:23.520
Yeah.

00:20:25.800 --> 00:20:27.870
How about we go there next?

00:20:29.680 --> 00:20:33.280
<i>Cheerleader Samurai vs. Megaton Shark</i>?

00:20:34.350 --> 00:20:36.480
This?

00:20:36.480 --> 00:20:38.370
Doesn't it look good?

00:20:38.370 --> 00:20:40.320
What do you think, Asuka?

00:20:40.990 --> 00:20:42.190
Fine with me, I guess.

00:20:42.190 --> 00:20:44.560
Okay, let's do it, then!

00:20:44.560 --> 00:20:46.030
I'll go get tickets to see it soon.

00:20:49.120 --> 00:20:50.120
Here you go.

00:20:52.800 --> 00:20:55.520
If Asuka-san's going...

00:20:55.520 --> 00:20:56.890
Yeah.

00:20:56.890 --> 00:20:59.200
Let's come back again, all four of us.

00:20:59.750 --> 00:21:01.500
Okay, see you later.

00:21:01.500 --> 00:21:02.930
Bye!

00:21:04.670 --> 00:21:06.580
I'll be going, then.

00:21:06.580 --> 00:21:07.390
See you.

00:21:09.730 --> 00:21:10.850
Asuka-san...

00:21:11.980 --> 00:21:13.790
Is school fun?

00:21:15.690 --> 00:21:16.730
Yeah.

00:21:16.730 --> 00:21:18.120
I think it is.

00:21:19.860 --> 00:21:22.760
That's why I don't want
to be a Magical Girl anymore.

00:21:23.240 --> 00:21:27.230
I don't want to lose any more
of the people close to me.

00:21:27.230 --> 00:21:28.900
Right...

00:21:30.680 --> 00:21:33.730
I'm glad you have friends here.

00:21:33.850 --> 00:21:35.620
See you tomorrow.

00:21:38.190 --> 00:21:41.810
<i></i>Not<i> fighting because you have
things you care about...</i>

00:21:41.810 --> 00:21:44.210
<i>You're supposed to do the
opposite, Asuka-san.</i>

00:21:58.050 --> 00:21:59.680
You're Makino Nozomi,

00:21:59.680 --> 00:22:04.090
daughter of Makino Akinori from
the Foreign Affairs Police, right?

00:22:14.110 --> 00:22:16.900
Now we have all the cards we need.

00:22:32.910 --> 00:22:35.370
I can't wait to see the movie.

00:24:12.450 --> 00:24:14.810
Nozomi was kidnapped, chu!

00:24:14.810 --> 00:24:17.200
Terrible torture or execution...

00:24:17.200 --> 00:24:20.220
Just imagining what she could be 
going through makes me shiver, chu!

00:24:20.220 --> 00:24:22.970
Next time, "Babel Brigade—Combat Begins."

00:24:20.520 --> 00:24:23.810
<b>Babel Brigade—Combat Begins</b>

00:24:22.970 --> 00:24:26.720
With your Magical Karambit,
rip the bad guys to pieces, chu!
